2 CONT
2 CONT - Heinrich Brüning. Burgess in Stockholm, Sweden in the 1400s [Mentioned from 1481 in Swedish sources]. In 1480 Heinrich is mentioned as an owner of a house on Mühlenstrasse 930 in Lübeck. This house is sold to a Wobbeke Salters i
2 CONC n 1482. Heinrich is mentioned as dead in 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Gerd Brünik, brother of Heinrich. Lived in 1489 on Holstenstrasse 299 as a guardian. He moved to Stockholm, Sweden and became a merchant burgess. He dies there sometime before 1518.  
2 CONT
2 CONT - Herman Brüning, brother of Gerd and Heinrich. He lived in Danzig in the end of the 1400s.
2 CONT
2 CONT An uncle of the above mentioned brothers was:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Herman Brüning, a burgess in Lübeck. He lived in 1473 in Lübeck. In 1475 he lived on Mengestrasse 43. In 1470 he had married N.N. Wyndelke [earlier married to a Hinrich Urvat]. He died in 1507 in Lübeck.
2 CONT
