1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Cronman
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/anrep/1/0501.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Johan Cronman (1662-1737)' was made a Baron in 1727, and both the Governor of Malmö and Commandant of Skane in 1727 (b. February 2, 1662; Ingermanland, Russia - d. July 26, 1737; Malmö, Skåne, Sweden) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: He was the son of Joakim Cronman (1638-1703) and Lunetta Makeléer (1639-1693). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Career: He was a Lieutenant with the Narva Garrison, and Second Captain with the Narke-Varmland regiment in 1687. He was promoted to Captain with Zurlauben's regiment in 1699, and made Lieutenant-Colonel in 1701. He was promoted t
2 CONC o Colonel of the Kronoberg regiment 1706, but was captured at Perovolochna and held prisoner until 1722. He was a Lieutenant-General of of the infantry in 1722. He was made a Baron in 1727, and named the County Governor of Malmö a
2 CONC nd Commandant of Skåne Province in 1727. He fought in 13 battles, and was never wounded. He spoke 8 languages: Swedish, Latin, German, Estonian, Polish, Russian, French and Dutch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: He was buried in Malmö, Skåne, Sweden. His epitaph at Saint Peter Church reads: "Thro Konigl:r Maij:ts Zu Schweden Wolbestalter Generallientenant der Infanterie Landes Hauptman und OberCommendannt der Festungen Zu Schonen 
2 CONC Hochwolgebohren Baron H:r Johan Cronman Freijherr Von Alatskivi Kadaster und Kakara Herr Von Vosuauer SattKula Gebohren Auf Alatskivi 1662 den 2 Novemb. Gelich Gestorben In Malmö den 26 Julii 1737." It translates into English as: 
2 CONC "His Royal Majesty of Sweden ..., Lieutenant General of the Infantry, Landes-Hauptman and High Commandant at the Fortress of Skåne, Honourable Baron Mr. Johan Cronman, Baron to Alatskivi, Kodafer and Kohora, Master of Wasuva and S
2 CONC ottkylä. Born at Alatskivi November 2, 1662. Died in Malmö on July 26, 1737."
