1 NAME Melker /von Falkenberg/
2 GIVN Melker
2 SURN von Falkenberg
2 _MARNM von Falkenberg
2 NICK Melchior
2 NICK Melcher
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1519
1 OCCU Överste, bror till Jürgen von Falkenberg som dog 1530, se Gottfrids stamtavla
1 TITL Överste
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Falkenberg_af_B%C3%A5lby_nr_105
2 CONT
2 CONT Melker von Falkenberg (son of Hans von Falkenberg, tab 1), to Schönermark and Heinrichsdorf. Was 1520 colonel for a regiment on horseback in Mark-Brandenburg. Married to Valborg von Sidau, daughter of Claus von Sidau and Emerentia
2 CONC  von Blanckenborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baltzar von Falkenberg. Heir to Schönermark, lord of Ermes and Salisburg in Livland. Came to Livland and became a country councillor in Livland in 1547 and marshal with the master Herman von Brüggeney. Died 1557. Married in 1549 t
2 CONC o Margareta von Blanckenfelt in her first marriage (married 2nd with Martin von Boldeck, who was murdered in 1563-06-10 at his home in Salisburg by his brother-in-law Frans and Christoffer von Blanckenfelt. Married 3:o with his br
2 CONC other-in-law the horseman of Swedish service Tomas von Boldeck) (At (Sch).), died in 1572, daughter of Polish knighthood in Livland hauptman Frans Joachimsson von Blanckenfelt, to Vollmar and Blanckenfeltshof, and Kunigunda von Ti
2 CONC esenhausen.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik von Falkenberg. Heir to Schönermark, Ermes and Salisburg, lord of Börstorp in Hassle parish, Skaraborg County, Trystorp in Tångeråsa parish and Bålby in Skagershults parish (both in Örebro County). Born 1553-02-01 in Livlan
2 CONC d. Came to Sweden in 1595. Colonel for the war people at Neuhausen 1601. Swedish War Council and Inspector General 1608. Knight of the Order of Germany in Livland. Swedish legacy to Mecklenburg, Kurpfaltz, Hessen-Cassel and Brauns
2 CONC chweig in 1611. Governor at Kalmar 1611. Died 1629 (1615) (NF.) 27/3 at Trystorp and is located next to his wife buried in Örebro church, each an epitafium with their and their anor's weapons and inscription etc., found in the cho
2 CONC ir to the left of the altar. Married in 1581 to Elisabet von Vietinghoff, of the house Ridlep, born 1559, died 1620-04-21, daughter of Conrad Arnoldsson von Vietinghoff, to Bidlep and Lemmets, and Gertrud Ottosdotter Yxkull, to Fi
2 CONC chtel and Padenorm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad von Falkenberg, naturalized Falkenberg af Trystorp , born 1591, died 1654. See the noble family Falkenberg af Trystorp no. 18, Tab 1. Melker von Falkenberg, naturalized Falkenberg af Bålby , born 1597, died 1651. See Tab. 3
2 CONC .
