2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Count (since 1779) '''Karl Johann Friedrich von Medem''' (March 29, 1762 in Mesothen, Duchy of Courland and Semigallia - November 26, 1827 in Mitau, Courland Governorate) - from the Baltic Germans a landowner of the Duchy of Courl
2 CONC and, Semigallia and Pilten, a member of the nobility's self-government. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born to Johann Friedrich von Medem and Louise Charlotte von Manteufel. Sister Ona Charlotte Dorothea (1761–1821), the last duchess of Curonian Spit, and brother Kristoforos (1763–1838), ambassador of the Russian Empire to the Unit
2 CONC ed States (1796–1808), grew up together. To the father in 1779 when the title of earl was granted, it also went to the children.
2 CONT
2 CONT After coming of age, Karl Johan Friedrich gradually took over part of his parents' estates. Curonian Spit: Remten and Vecauć (since 1786), Zante (Santen) (1791-93), Vytinius (Veitenfeld) and Dselsen (since 1793), Lielauć, Gailenho
2 CONC f and Kėvelė (Keweln, since 1802), Jaunaucė (since 1804) and Bėnė (Banen, since 1818); In Lithuania: Medemrodė (from 1804), Eglesius and Ivanauskius (around 1820) and from 1804 the now extinct Carlsfeld, as well as the manors of O
2 CONC ld Žagare, Šakyna. in 1826 established the first evangelical Lutheran house of prayer in the house he owned in Senoja Žagare.
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1796 was elected as a representative of the nobles of Tukum County to the Self-Governing Committee of the Curonian Nobles. in 1797 The nobles of Mintauja county had elected him as their marshal. Headed the Curonian Lantag (Parl
2 CONC iament) in 1799, 1803, 1807, 1813. and in 1814. He was one of the initiators of the founding of the higher school "Academia Petrina" in Mintauja. In 1812 led the government of the independent Duchy of Courland, Semigallia and Pilt
2 CONC en established by Napoleon's army. in 1817 In St. Petersburg, he successfully conducted negotiations on the abolition of serfdom in the Courland Governorate, and also achieved the abolition of some taxes in the region.
2 CONT
2 CONT Assessment 
2 CONT
2 CONT Order of St. Anne, First Class (Russian Empire) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
