2 NOTE Here we can see the family crest of Jan van Galen as we can also see in many of his portraits, always in the left or right corner above him. His family came from the city Dinklage and when we look at the crest / coat of arms of th
3 CONC e city Dinklage, we can see exact the same symbol as Jan van Galen did use in his family crest. It is the symbol in the middle/centre, it looks like a fish hook. I believe this means that the family Von/Van Galen has a very close 
3 CONC relation to the city Dinklage, perhaps they were once Lords over that city ?  
3 CONT http://www.maritiemdigitaal.nl/index.cfm?event=search.getdetail&amp...... 
3 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinklage
