1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carl Gustaf Creutz deltog i striderna  i Halmstad, Lund och Landskrona. Han uppges ha varit en av Karl XII:s bäste krigare och hade en blind lydnad för kungen. Han deltog i slaget vid Poltava 1709 och tillfångatogs
2 CONC  av ryssarna när Karl XII:s arme kapitulerade  i Perevolotjna. Deltog samma år i tsar Peters segertåg (förnedringståget av tillfångatagna karoliner) i Moskva. Han kunde återvända till Sverige 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.helsinki.fi/ylioppilasmatrikkeli/henkilo.php?id=U353
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=15651
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Gustaf_Creutz
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Creutz_nr_48#TAB_21
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Gustaf Creutz (1660−1728) was a Swedish general.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Gustaf Creutz was the youngest son of Lorentz Creutz Sr. and Elsa Jacob Daughter Duwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as a page of Charles XI and experienced the Scanian War. By 1691 he was a captain in the Household Cavalry Regiment under Charles XII. The Great Northern War began in 1700 and Creutz landing in Zealand . He distinguished
2 CONC  himself at the Battle of the Pechora and at the battle of Kletsk (in present day Poland).  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Kletsk_(1706)
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointment to Major and Lieutenant Colonel then came quickly. Carl Gustaf became colonel in 1704. The Battle of Poltava in 1709 brought Creutz command of the entire cavalry, however, he had to surrender soon after Perevolotnya. A
2 CONC fter Count Piper's death, he was the senior Swedish prisoner in Russia, of which his extant correspondence bears visible witness. In 1722, he was able to return to Sweden and service in the cavalry.
1 FAMS @F6000000004161000288@
1 RFN geni:6000000004160609904
1 SUBM @S6000000004160920145@
